Z||000012||PearlBlueSoul||12-22-2000||07:48 PM||||you know, his parents need to give him a thorough spanking.  make that ass red as a Fiero's paint. <P>For those who don't know, Ford used either different heads or fuel maps...summin like that in the T-bird V8s (5.0 or 4.6). they basically detuned them and made them low output.  Regardless if it was a Mustang motor, it's still detuned like luke warm tea.  <P>Therefore:<BR>a 4.6 V8 auto stock is SLOW AS F!@#.  A friend of mine had a 5.0 V8, and although we never raced I'm near positive it wasn't much faster than my deuce.  Wouldn't suprise me in the least if it was a duke that was keeping up.  those cars are slow.  Give that guy a corner and give the fiero corners.  he'd get eaten alive faster than a goldfish in a whale.  <P>glad I don't act like that.  Kids liek that give us a bad generation stereotype.<P><BR>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">         <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.<P>[This message has been edited by PearlBlueSoul (edited 12-22-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by PearlBlueSoul (edited 12-22-2000).]||||reg||1
